+The target evaluation corpora are AAEC and CDCP, with CDCP multi-premise relations retained as native hyperedges. The specification fixes center selection, protected candidates, proposal scheduling, a genuinely sequential baseline, and relaxed oracle sets. An independent reference program passes 19 checks on constructed objects. Exhaustive enumeration of a four-component graph demonstrates that a newly legal nonincident relation need not be recovered in the same transaction; sequential commits can also reduce total utility. These findings concern specification consistency and mechanism boundaries, not corpus performance. Training gains, the incremental benefit of joint repair, and interaction between the two stages remain unsupported by completed multi-seed corpus experiments.
 
